223 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 92 0 R
/T (Modern systems generate a huge number of log messages, making it difficult to identify failures and understand where they started. This project develops an unsupervised log analysis framework that learns normal system behavior and detects unusual and previously unseen patterns by looking at the meaning, structure, and behavior of logs. The system also explains why an event was considered abnormal, identifies the components that are likely involved, and presents the results through a dashboard to help engineers investigate problems more easily.)
/E (Modern systems generate a huge number of log messages, making it difficult to identify failures and understand where they started. This project develops an unsupervised log analysis framework that learns normal system behavior and detects unusual and previously unseen patterns by looking at the meaning, structure, and behavior of logs. The system also explains why an event was considered abnormal, identifies the components that are likely involved, and presents the results through a dashboard to help engineers investigate problems more easily.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
